WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.380
My dad worked . . . and I don't know what year he started at the plant.

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:12.520
I don't even know what my dad before he went to the plants . . . He was working at a plant called Cit-Con.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.700
But he worked as a janitor.

4
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:21.060
He raised thirteen kids on a janitor’s job and digging wells.

5
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.760
That's . . . My dad was out at the plant for over thirty-five years as a janitor.

6
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:33.200
He even plant a garden at the plant and the people was eating from the garden he planted at the plant.

7
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.140
He was bringing food home, not knowing.

8
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:42.480
Because of the ignorance of not knowing how horrible chemicals were, he had a garden out there.

9
00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:50.600
At the same time we were eating that stuff and the people there were eating it because until today people don't realize how horrible chemicals are.

10
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:56.920
. . . We been in a fight for the plants ever since the first one got there.

11
00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:03.100
My brothers and them couldn't understand why the plants were moving in on us.

12
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.680
They had been fighting ever since I was a child.

13
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:12.200
Then when I got old enough I began to fight with them for . . . Is these plants causing the cancer,

14
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.920
and the asthma, and the kidney failure?

15
00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.680
And then of course we all realized that they were bringing jobs.

16
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:24.100
Every time we found out about industry it was always an undercover thing.

17
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.760
They went and took some older person off aside and offered them some money for their land,

18
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:37.700
and the older people didn't understand what they were doing and the people . . . God forgive me, that's just what white folks did.

19
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:42.380
If they take a black person with . . . Uneducated, didn't know nothing about business,

20
00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:48.740
and they took for granted . . . They took them for granted on their ignorance about buying out stuff.

21
00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:55.200
So a lot of our older people sold land to industries not understanding what they were doing.

22
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:58.420
All they know is that back then the money was hard to get.

23
00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:05.520
And somebody come along and offer you some money that you had, they was quick to sell the property.
